# Intentionally empty.
#
# Write access to this repo is already limited to the org owners, which is a narrower set
# than the application repo it was split out of. A code-owner rule on top of that would add
# nothing: everyone who can push here is an admin, and admins bypass review unless the branch
# rule also disallows bypassing — so the requirement would be a convention among the same
# handful of people, not a control.
#
# It becomes worth adding the day someone outside the org owners curates these documents:
# create a team, grant it Write (Read is silently ignored — GitHub treats an owner without
# write access as unresolvable and requests nobody), enable "Require review from Code Owners"
# on main, and uncomment the line below.
#
# Own `*` rather than the documents alone, so that this file and the CI workflow are covered
# by the same rule; otherwise one PR can remove the requirement and change policy together.
#
# * @RunOnFlux/policy-owners
